### JSON Structure
```json
{
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "version": "1.0",
  "strings": {
    "system.page.title": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "System budgets"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "translation.system.page.title": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "ar": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "ميزانيات النظام"
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "System budgets"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Key Format & Examples

**Keys are dot-separated paths.** The system supports two naming patterns:
- Web-style unprefixed: `system.page.title`, `error.loadFailed`
- Translation-prefixed: `translation.system.page.title`, `translation.error.loadFailed`

**Both variants exist** in the xcstrings file (web keys used by native components, translation.* variants auto-generated during i18n sync).

