### How TSPageTitle Resolves Localization

**File:** `/Users/atulgupta/Documents/repos/.teslasync-parallel/20260615-130844-89414/slot-3/apps/apple/Sources/Components/UI/Typography.swift:37-49`

```swift
public struct TSPageTitle: View {
  private let text: LocalizedStringKey  // Takes LocalizedStringKey, not String
  
  public init(_ text: LocalizedStringKey) {
    self.text = text
  }
  
  public var body: some View {
    Text(text)  // SwiftUI's Text(LocalizedStringKey) automatically resolves from bundle
      .font(Font.TS.display)
      .foregroundStyle(Color.TS.textPrimary)
      .accessibilityAddTraits(.isHeader)
  }
}
```

**Resolution chain:**
1. `TSPageTitle("system.page.title")` — caller passes the key as a `LocalizedStringKey`
2. SwiftUI's `Text()` init with `LocalizedStringKey` automatically:
   - Searches `Localizable.xcstrings` for the key
   - Respects device language + region settings
   - Falls back to the key itself if not found
3. **Key MUST exist in xcstrings** or it renders verbatim (e.g., "system.page.title" shows as text)

**Example usage from SystemPage:**
```swift
// /Users/atulgupta/Documents/repos/.teslasync-parallel/20260615-130844-89414/slot-3/apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/SystemPage.swift:45
TSPageTitle("system.page.title")
// Resolves to "System budgets" from xcstrings entry
```

