## 8. SSE / LIVE POLLING & STALENESS (ADR-013)

### LiveConnection API - `/Users/atulgupta/Documents/repos/.teslasync-parallel/20260615-130844-89414/slot-3/apps/apple/Sources/SharedFacade/LiveConnection.swift:1-77`

```swift
// Connection state (ADR-013: stale flag when no event/heartbeat in freshness window)
public enum LiveConnectionState: Equatable, Sendable {
  case connecting
  case open                // Live, fresh data
  case reconnecting
  case stale               // Open BUT >2min since last event/heartbeat
  case closed
  
  public var hasUsableData: Bool {
    switch self {
    case .open, .stale, .reconnecting: true
    case .connecting, .closed: false
    }
  }
}

// Event kind discriminator
public enum LiveEventKind: Equatable, Sendable {
  case connected, heartbeat, vehicleUpdate, alert, exportStatus, achievementUnlocked, signal, unknown
}

// Live event projection
public struct LiveEvent {
  public let id: String?
  public let kind: LiveEventKind
  public let raw: Shared.LiveEvent  // Retains original KMP event for payload access
  
  public init(_ event: Shared.LiveEvent)
  private static func classify(_ event: Shared.LiveEvent) -> LiveEventKind
}
```

### Polling Pattern (Concrete Example)

**File:** `/Users/atulgupta/Documents/repos/.teslasync-parallel/20260615-130844-89414/slot-3/apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/RedisSignalViewerPage.swift` (polling loop for 5s refresh):

```swift
/// Drives the web `refetchInterval: INTERVALS.REALTIME` (5s) while auto-refresh is armed
/// and a vehicle is selected. Tied to the view lifecycle via `.task(id:)`, so it cancels
/// when the toggle flips, the vehicle changes, or the page disappears.
private func runAutoRefresh() async {
  guard model.autoRefresh, model.hasSelection else { return }
  while !Task.isCancelled {
    try? await Task.sleep(nanoseconds: 5 * 1_000_000_000)  // 5s
    if Task.isCancelled { break }
    await model.refreshSignals()
  }
}
```

**Usage in view:**
```swift
.task { 
  if case .loaded = model.vehiclesState { return }
  await model.load()
}
.task(id: model.selectedVehicleID) {
  await model.loadSignals()
}
.task(id: RedisAutoRefreshKey(vehicleID: model.selectedVehicleID, enabled: model.autoRefresh)) {
  await runAutoRefresh()  // 5s polling loop
}
```

### Staleness Display

**LoadableState carries stale flag:**
```swift
public enum LoadableState<Value> {
  case loading(cached: Value?, stale: Bool)
  case loaded(Value, stale: Bool)
  case empty(stale: Bool)
  case failed(FacadeError, cached: Value?, stale: Bool)
  
  public var isStale: Bool {
    switch self {
    case .idle: false
    case let .loading(_, stale), let .loaded(_, stale),
         let .empty(stale), let .failed(_, _, stale):
      stale
    }
  }
}
```

**Stale banner component:**
```swift
// /Users/atulgupta/Documents/repos/.teslasync-parallel/20260615-130844-89414/slot-3/apps/apple/Sources/Components/Feedback/Banners.swift:112-121
public struct TSLiveStaleDataBanner: View {
  public init() {}
  public var body: some View {
    TSAlertBanner(
      tone: .warning,
      systemImage: "clock.badge.exclamationmark",
      title: "stale.title",
      message: "stale.message"
    )
  }
}
```

**Usage in page:**
```swift
if model.state.isStale {
  TSLiveStaleDataBanner()
}
```

The `stale` boolean flows from the shared-core `Resource<T>.stale` field (set when SSE heartbeat/event >2min old, ADR-013) and propagates through `LoadableState.from(resource)` transformer.

